# RME LAB fee approval and billing integrity (rule 246)

Owner decisions 2026-11-20: DL-LAB, DL-SNAP, A-01/REV-02, A-02/REV-03, A-04, A-08, A-22, A-23, A-24, A-25, A-29,
REV-01, REV-04. Spec: `docs/architecture/rme-lab-financial-state-machine.md`. Decision record:
`docs/decisions/rme-lab-fee-approval-1-owner-design-lock.md`. Findings: FIN-01, FIN-02, FIN-03, FIN-04, FIN-05, FIN-06.

## Current state (verified 2026-11-20)

No LAB-fee classification exists; a free-text line may carry any price; HAS_LAB is read live from
`mst_treatments.requires_lab`; no CHECK guards item money or invoice totals beyond the NO_CHARGE trio. This is
implementation drift against this rule until it is implemented.

## Locked target — the only LAB fee route

1. A LAB fee is an item with `line_kind = 'LAB_FEE'` and a positive subtotal (A-24), linked by `lab_for_item_id` to a
   line on the same invoice whose `requires_lab_snapshot` is true, and referencing exactly one LAB-fee approval
   (`lab_fee_approval_id`, unique).
2. Before issuance a maker requests the approval for the visit (branch, patient, visit, LAB line, exact amount); a
   designated branch checker who is neither the maker nor the issuing cashier approves (rule 247). Issuance consumes one
   APPROVED, unexpired, unrevoked approval whose fingerprint matches the priced LAB line, once, inside the issuance
   transaction.
3. No other route: never a free-text line; never an invoice correction, even with an approval (REV-01); never a
   supplementary or replacement invoice (REV-04); never a lab-domain (`trx_invoices`) charge.
4. A correction refuses to add, change or remove a LAB_FEE line and refuses to switch a line's treatment to or from a
   LAB-requiring treatment (A-29).

## Snapshots

5. Items snapshot `line_kind`, `requires_lab_snapshot`, treatment code and name at issue and at correction apply;
   candidate generation and backfill read the snapshot; a master edit never changes an issued invoice.

## Money and invariants

6. Integer cents; `item.subtotal` is NET; `trx_rme_invoices.subtotal` is GROSS; `grand_total = Σ item.subtotal`;
   no tax. L = Σ NET of LAB_FEE items; NN = Σ NET of other items; G = grand_total.
7. Inv1, no exception (A-22): L > 0 → NN > 0. An invoice with a positive LAB fee and NN = 0 is never issued.
8. Inv2, normal rule: HAS_LAB ∧ NN = 0 → L = 0 ∧ status REVERSED.
   Inv2, owner amendment A-02: an invoice with HAS_LAB ∧ NN = 0 ∧ L = 0 may be issued only by consuming one GRANTED,
   unexpired, unrevoked Owner LAB issuance exception bound to that visit and to the exact priced lines (fingerprint),
   approved in-system by an identity on the source-controlled owner allowlist (never by role or permission, so never by
   Super Admin as such), expiring at most 7 days after approval, citing a reason code from the owner's closed list
   (A-25), single-use, with immutable evidence. The amendment never relaxes Inv1.
   The route stays disabled (fail-closed, `LAB_EXCEPTION_ROUTE_DISABLED`) until the operational Rp0 LAB invoice flow —
   visit closure and lab-candidate generation for a G = 0 invoice, which S6-Q2 keeps out of NO_CHARGE — is designed,
   approved and implemented (A-23, DES-LAB-RP0).
9. Inv3 (A-04): G = 0 ∧ correction_version > 0 → status REVERSED; an unclassified historical row may instead cite an
   approved historical exception.
10. Legitimate initial Rp0 invoices without LAB are never rejected. Unclassified historical invoices are exempt from
    Inv1/Inv2 by an explicit predicate; `historical_exception_id` is allowed only on unclassified rows.
11. Database part: CHECKs verify single-row facts only (presence of an approval or exception reference, totals
    arithmetic, positive LAB_FEE subtotal). Approval and exception validity, single use and cross-row totals are
    verified by the service under the lock and by deferred constraint triggers owned by the object owner (rule 245).
    CHECKs are added NOT VALID and validated after an owner-run data audit.

## Acceptance criteria

- Every row of the invariant matrix and of the test matrix in the spec passes on PostgreSQL 16; while the route is
  disabled every exception attempt is refused with `LAB_EXCEPTION_ROUTE_DISABLED`.
- A LAB_FEE line without a consumed approval, a zero LAB_FEE line, a free-text LAB fee, a correction touching a LAB_FEE
  line and a correction switching to or from a LAB-requiring treatment are each refused with a stable code and audited
  after rollback.
- Flipping `requires_lab` after issue leaves HAS_LAB, candidates and totals of issued invoices unchanged.
- Direct SQL violating Inv1, Inv2, Inv3 or the positive LAB_FEE rule fails with SQLSTATE 23514; every CHECK shows
  `convalidated = true` after the data audit.

## Unchanged

Rule 194 manual pricing (free-text non-LAB lines stay allowed), D21c pending, rule 217 NO_CHARGE (S6-Q2), D23/PP-8, D28.
